[size=5][b]Bulk Sell Equipment[/b][/size]
Finds the appraised talismans you no longer need and sells them all at once. It works the same way the game's [b]View/Sell Equipment[/b] screen does, with the same price and the same game calls.

This version sells [b]appraised talismans only[/b] (Unknown / Historical / Secret / Golden Age Charm, rarity 5-8). Weapons, armor and crafted talismans are never touched.

[size=4][b]What it sells[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Covered talismans[/b]: a talisman you keep has every skill at the same or a higher level, and slots that fit the same decorations. Weapon and armor slots are compared separately.
[*][b]Duplicates[/b]: identical copies beyond the one that is kept.
[*][b]Rarity rule[/b] (optional): everything up to a chosen rarity, except talismans with skills you mark as kept.
[/list]
Before anything is sold, every talisman is listed with its price, its verdict and the talisman kept instead. You get the game's own price (1,500 / 3,000 / 4,500 / 8,000 z for rarity 5 / 6 / 7 / 8). Every run writes a JSON receipt.

[size=4][b]Never sold[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The equipped talisman, and talismans used in any loadout
[*]Favorites
[*]Talismans with decorations attached
[*]Crafted talismans
[*]Talismans with an RNG Charm Crafting Set/Group bonus
[/list]
A confirmation only sells the list it showed: if the rules change or the box is scanned again first, it is withdrawn. Before you confirm, it lists any skill whose best level would go down. Each talisman is checked again right before it is sold, and anything that changed since the scan is skipped. Selling waits while a game menu is open or the game is saving. A run stops on its own if zenny does not go up by exactly the expected amount. If a game update removes a function the mod relies on, or RNG Charm Crafting's bonus file cannot be read, selling turns off by itself and says why.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]REFramework (a recent nightly build is recommended)
[*]Tested on Steam build 24705561 (October 2026)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]Fluffy Mod Manager[/b]: import the zip without unpacking it, then enable [i]Bulk Sell Equipment[/i].
[b]Manual[/b]: copy the [i]reframework[/i] folder from the zip into the game folder (next to MonsterHunterWilds.exe).

[size=4][b]How to use[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Stand in the field or at camp with no game menu open, then press [b]Insert[/b].
[*]Open [b]Script Generated UI > Bulk Sell Equipment > Show window[/b].
[*]Click [b]Scan Equipment Box[/b], then pick your rules and review the list.
[*]Optionally, click [b]Sell just 1 (test)[/b] first. Then click [b]Sell N talismans > Yes, sell[/b].
[*]Let the game autosave, for example by fast travelling.
[/list]
[b]Sales cannot be undone. Back up your save first.[/b] Sales are written to disk at the game's next autosave. If you close the game before then, they are not kept.

[size=4][b]Files[/b][/size]
Settings: [i]reframework/data/BulkSell/config.json[/i]
Receipts: [i]reframework/data/BulkSell/receipts/[/i]

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Crafted talismans are not used when deciding what is covered.
[*]The covered check does not count decorations you could still slot in. Decoration-aware comparison is planned.
[*]The interface is in English. Skill names follow your game language.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Source and bug reports[/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/zamcoder/bulk-sell-equipment-mhwilds]github.com/zamcoder/bulk-sell-equipment-mhwilds[/url]
When reporting a bug, please attach your receipt file and the REFramework log ([i]re2_framework_log.txt[/i] in the game folder).

